## Why This Is Asked

This question probes understanding of secure multi-tenant design, auditable operations, and basic access control in a beginner-friendly setting.

## Key Concepts

- JWT-based auth with tenant_id boundaries
- Row-Level Security or tenant-scoped data stores
- Immutable/append-only audit log with canonical fields
- Model versioning exposure and validation
- End-to-end test strategy for security and data isolation

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo middleware to verify JWT and enforce tenant boundary
function authorize(req) {
  const token = req.headers['authorization'];
  const payload = verifyJwt(token);
  if (!payload || payload.tenant_id !== req.params.tenant_id) throw new Error('Unauthorized');
  return payload;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate audit logs to detect tampering?
- How would you rotate signing keys without downtime?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests understanding of privacy-preserving experimentation at an API boundary and how to build deterministic, auditable feature variants into an existing compute API.

## Key Concepts

- Deterministic hashing (HMAC) for stable variant assignment
- Data masking (user_id_masked) to protect PII
- Experiment design (experiment_id, variant) and minimal integration with cca_score
- API design, observability, and simple test strategies

## Code Example

```javascript
const crypto = require('crypto');
function variantFor(userId, experimentId, secret){
  const hash = crypto.createHmac('sha256', secret).update(userId + '-' + experimentId).digest('hex');
  const n = parseInt(hash.slice(0, 8), 16);
  return (n % 2 === 0) ? 'A' : 'B';
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you extend to more than two variants while preserving determinism?
- How would you validate fairness and detect potential leakage across experiments?

## Why This Is Asked
This tests designing a compliant, scalable, multi-tenant cca_score system with strong isolation and auditability.

## Key Concepts
- Tenant isolation via partitioned feature stores
- Per-tenant key management and encryption
- Explainability safety and PII redaction
- Immutable auditing and breach-testing

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode: tenant-scoped scoring
function scoreForTenant(tenantId, payload, store, modelReg) {
  const part = store.getPartition(tenantId);
  const features = part.fetchFeatures(payload);
  const model = modelReg.getModel(tenantId);
  return model.predict(features);
}
```

